  "routeAdjustment": "Reuse the checked external coefficient argument on the existing literal j, eta and Eisenstein series. Replace its modular-polynomial package input with the already proved original monic relation. This removes the irreducibility dependency from prime nonmembership and avoids duplicating analytic modularity.",
  "discharged": "The original j series has positive coefficients at every nonnegative index, by its literal Eisenstein numerator and eta inverse. The root-of-unity orbit and Vieta coefficient identity rule out j(q^p)=P(j(q)) over every characteristic-zero coefficient field. The already proved prime monic relation gives integrality over the polynomial j-algebra; native integral-root descent then proves that the actual prime j substitution is outside the rational j-field. No nonmembership, coefficient positivity or irreducibility premise remains.",
  "remaining": "Prime conjugate-product irreducibility and exact degree are the next consumers. All-level generation and exact j-map degree, modular ramification and fiber counts, analytic cusp-form realization and downstream period, arithmetic and symmetric-power gates remain required. DUB-17--20 OPEN; 16/20.",
